        {
          "role": "Preferred",
          "context": "Editor",
          "proposedMacos": "Cmd+3",
          "keyToken": "Primary-3",
          "actionTarget": "LuaAction/script-19",
          "implementationType": "Profile Lua",
          "mappingClass": "Similar",
          "availability": "Lua accessible",
          "note": "No Live-style triplet toggle action. Building blocks: EditorSnap/grid-type-thirds|sixths|twelfths|twentyfourths -- the Snap radio actions are registered per editing context, so Editor:access_action must name the \"EditorSnap\" group, not \"Snap\". set_grid_type is not Lua-exported. StepEditing/toggle-triplet is step-entry only and must not be used. Implemented as profile/scripts/ardoton_toggle_triplet_grid.lua at Lua action slot 19, bound in profile/keybindings/macos/ardour.keys as Editor Primary-3. The binding lives in the Editor context, not the shared Editing set: Ardour copies the Editing bindings per editing context and prefixes every action name with the context name (Bindings::relativize), so a LuaAction target there can never resolve. The stock Global Primary-3 -> Transport/ToggleFollowEdits binding is removed by the profile; it consumed the chord before the Editor context saw it, and no sourceId claims it. Verified end-to-end against Ardour 9.7 for all four binary/triplet pairs in both directions, plus the documented no-op on the shipped GridTypeBeatDiv32 default.",
          "status": "Implemented",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "kind": "Action registration",
              "claim": "Target exists",
              "result": "Confirmed",
              "reference": "../ardour@9.7:gtk2_ardour/editor_actions.cc:544 (LuaAction/script-1..32 are registered unconditionally for every Ardour session, independent of whether a script is assigned to the slot)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "E2E test",
              "claim": "Behavior verified",
              "reference": "tests/e2e/test_editing_shortcuts.py:test_triplet_grid_round_trips",
              "result": "Confirmed"
